//? Title: Super-resolution:five architectures with visible tensor optimization
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Construct genuine x2 CIFAR degradation pairs with antialiased Keys bicubic tensors. Explain CRD shuffle,RCAN channel gates and VDSR adjustable clipping,then run all five full/compact graphs. Show every optimizer update for SRCNN,ESPCN,VDSR,EDSR and RCAN,restore independent prediction-only stores,and compare all32 held-out images on identical studio-range Y coordinates against unchanged bicubic.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.8_other_vision_tasks/super_resolution.cpp`.

> The method

The observation is a genuine16x16 downsampled image. Models either consume that LR grid or a bicubic32 interpolation derived from it. Training targets remain original32x32 pixels. Reusable tensor APIs own forward mechanisms and data transformations;the report explicitly owns optimizers,loops and checkpoint selection. Only evaluation/display clips predictions. No fitted baseline is hidden:the bicubic reference is fixed interpolation.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/super_resolution_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/super_resolution_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/super_resolution_concept.tikz > build/super_resolution_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/super_resolution_concept.svg build/super_resolution_concept.dvi > build/super_resolution_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
