\alttext(RCAN predictions compared with unchanged bicubic and genuine HR targets.)

VDSR reaches26.724774dB versus bicubic26.711192dB,a small.013582dB
difference on this32-image subset. Its SSIM is.855048 versus.854135.
The other four models have lower test PSNR and SSIM than bicubic. No.05dB
benchmark improvement is established. VDSR clips zero coordinates here:its
maximum raw derivative.001174 stays below the.1 bound. The clipping fixture
above exercises the mechanism when it is active.

A falling training objective does not establish recovered high-frequency
detail on new images. Compare every model with the fixed bicubic line and
inspect every held-out tile. The preview’s enlargement only makes original
pixels visible;it does not increase their information. These compact fits
preserve architectural mechanisms without claiming paper-level accuracy.

> Conclusion

Tensor degradation,permutation,attention and derivative clipping establish the local mechanisms. Five complete graphs and240 explicit optimizer steps connect these mechanisms to original image data. Common-coordinate held-out metrics,unchanged bicubic and every prediction tile keep short-fit claims measurable.

> References

- [Dong et al.,Image Super-Resolution Using Deep Convolutional Networks](https://arxiv.org/abs/1501.00092).
- [Shi et al.,Real-Time Single Image and Video Super-Resolution Using an Efficient Sub-Pixel Convolutional Neural Network](https://arxiv.org/abs/1609.05158).
- [Kim et al.,Accurate Image Super-Resolution Using Very Deep Convolutional Networks](https://cv.snu.ac.kr/research/VDSR/).
- [Lim et al.,Enhanced Deep Residual Networks for Single Image Super-Resolution](https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.02921).
- [Zhang et al.,Image Super-Resolution Using Very Deep Residual Channel Attention Networks](https://arxiv.org/abs/1807.02758).
- [Wang et al.,official SSIM paper and implementation](https://ece.uwaterloo.ca/~z70wang/research/ssim/).
